  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations to Oregon reached $2.4B in FY2026 to date. The procurement environment delivered 12,989 awards, with an average award size of $185K, and obligations were up 15.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1.1B so far, followed by the Department of Agriculture with $537M. Ship Building and Repairing is the largest industry by obligations at $605M, while VIGOR MARINE LLC is the top vendor with $582M. Fiscal-year comparisons show a rise from $1.8B in FY21 to a peak of $2.5B in FY23, with FY24 and FY25 at $2.4B and $2.1B respectively, and FY26 returning to $2.4B. Contracting covers marine, forestry support, aircraft parts, civil construction, and transportation services, reflecting a mix of defense, infrastructure, and natural-resources work. These totals are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial. Use these figures to prioritize agency outreach and target industries where Oregon already has scale and momentum.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Oregon changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations were up 15.2% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year totals moved from $1.8B in FY21 to $2.5B in FY23, then to $2.4B in FY24, $2.1B in FY25, and $2.4B in FY26. The count of awards reached 12,989 in FY2026 to date with an average award size of $185K. These figures show where spending rose and which years held higher totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for the largest shares of Oregon contracting?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.1B in FY2026 to date and is the single largest buyer. The Department of Agriculture obligated $537M, and the Departments of Transportation, Homeland Security, and Veterans Affairs obligated $156M, $128M, and $127M respectively. Ship Building and Repairing accounted for $605M in obligations and Support Activities for Forestry accounted for $276M. VIGOR MARINE LLC is the top vendor with $582M, followed by COLLINS ELBIT VISION SYSTEMS, LLC at $196M."
      }
    ]
  },
